# supervised the research and are recorded in the Zenodo deposition as
# contributors with the "Supervisor" role (see .zenodo.json). CFF 1.2.0
# has no typed-contributor field, so the distinction cannot be expressed
# here; .zenodo.json is authoritative for the archived record.
authors:
  - family-names: "Proaño Morales"
    given-names: "Jonathan Josué"
    affiliation: "Facultad de Posgrado, Universidad de Salamanca"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7140-5318"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jonathan-Pm2/Floccus"
url: "https://github.com/Jonathan-Pm2/Floccus"
abstract: >-
  Floccus is a reproducible PRISMA 2020-compliant pipeline for systematic
  literature reviews on the mathematical modeling of biological floc dynamics
  in aquaculture and wastewater treatment systems. It integrates multi-source
  bibliographic ingestion (Scopus, Web of Science, IEEE Xplore, SciELO,
  enriched via OpenAlex and Europe PMC), three-layer deduplication
  (deterministic, semantic via dense embeddings on Qdrant HNSW, LLM-judged
  reconciliation), and a LangGraph-orchestrated screening agent that evaluates
  eleven binary PRISMA criteria with an asymmetric AND/OR rule. A second-pass
  LLM screening uses enriched metadata (OpenAlex topics and Europe PMC MeSH
  terms) for blind dual review of borderline records. All decisions carry a
  textual audit trail for human verification.
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - PRISMA 2020
  - large language models
  - LangGraph
  - biofloc
  - activated sludge
  - aquaculture
  - wastewater treatment
  - deduplication
  - dense embeddings
  - bibliographic data
